    "title": "'Tom Dooley' opens in July at Benton Hall in North Wilkesboro - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Rehearsals are underway for the 24th Season of “Tom Dooley: A Wilkes County Legend” at Benton Hall, 300 D Street, North Wilkesboro. The play is being produced as a partnership between Wilkes Playmakers and Bleu Moon Productions. The story was originally made famous by The New York Herald, who covered Tom Dula’s hanging. Later, Tom “Dooley’s” woeful tale was made internationally famous by The Kingston Trio’s ballad that is still well known today. Playwright and Director Karen Reynolds, used both The New York Herald’s article, the famous song, archived court records and interviews with many of the families still living in Elkville to write the play. The story not only concentrates on the famous lover’s triangle of Tom Dula, Laura Foster and Anne Melton — but is a celebration of Wilkes County’s folkways and superstitions. The singing duo, Magnolia Fire is back, and will perform music 30 minutes prior to each show as well as between scenes throughout the entire play. Performance dates are July 10, 11, 12, 17, 18, 19 at 7 p.m., and July 13 and July 20, at 3 p.m. Go to www.TomDooleyNC.com for tickets. Tickets can also be purchased at the door on a first come, first serve basis.",
